leted-example PDFs.Free basic builder exports in PDF, DOCX, and plain text.No watermark or surprise download charge.Optional paid assistance and advanced features disclosed upfront.These are proposed facilities; the templates and builder have not been created yet.5. The facilities job seekers should receiveThe full product should support the application journey without overwhelming the homepage.TableFacilityCustomer benefitPriorityTemplate libraryStart with a suitable documentLaunchRole-specific examplesUnderstand what to writeLaunchGuided resume builderTurn experience into an editable documentLaunchPDF, DOCX, and text exportsApply and make future changesLaunchResume checkFind specific, explainable issuesLaunchJob-description comparisonIdentify relevant evidence and possible gapsLaunchHuman review / rewriteGet personal assistanceLaunchCover-letter builderProduce a coordinated applicationNextMultiple resume versionsTailor without losing the master copyNextApplication trackerRecord applications, versions, and follow-upsNextLinkedIn copy assistanceAlign public positioningNextInterview preparationPractise questions based on real experienceLaterAchievement journalSave useful evidence before the next job searchLaterAdditional languages and marketsSupport local application conventionsLater, after testingImportant detailsFor first-time applicants: allow education, projects, volunteering, caregiving-related transferable experience, and part-time work without demanding a current job title.For career changers: help explain transferable evidence while preserving an honest employment history.For returning applicants: make gap explanations optional. Do not pressure people to disclose health or family information.For everyone: never invent skills, employers, qualifications, revenue figures, or promotions.I would avoid automatic mass application submission. Helping someone prepare a relevant application is a better initial product than sending many unreviewed applications on their 